316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (and decision-making. The A* algorithm is used to determine the optimal route by considering distance and path cost, ensuring efficient navigation. Linear Regression is applied to predict delivery time based on features such as distance, traffic level, and package weight, which helps in estimating accurate arrival times. Logistic Regression classifies routes into safe and risky categories, improving delivery reliability. K-Nearest Neighbors \(KNN\) identifies similar delivery patterns using historical data, which enhances decision support. K-Means clustering groups delivery areas to improve route planning and reduce operational complexity. The Decision Tree model selects the most suitable transport mode based on conditions like distance, traffic, and package size.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
